# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback. With react-router-dom owning client-side routing,
# any deep-link (e.g. /learn/patterns/secret-scanner) must serve index.html so the
# JS bundle can boot and the router can pick up the URL. Without this rule, refreshing
# on a non-root URL hits a 404 because Pages has no matching file on disk.
#
# Static assets (/assets/*, *.svg, *.txt, *.xml, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, etc.) are
# matched by their actual files first — Pages serves the SPA fallback only when no
# real file matches the request path.

